                              "scene_title": "Meeting Roger de Flor",
                              "setup": "After the bandit attack, Francisco is formally introduced to Roger de Flor, the legendary leader of the Catalan Company. In the train's dining car, Roger shares wine and war stories with his men while sizing up Francisco's potential. The mercenaries reveal their complex brotherhood forged in countless battles, while Roger explains their mission and Francisco's crucial role in finding Cicero's lost books.",
                              "symbolism": "The shared wine represents the bonds of brotherhood Francisco is joining. Roger's battle-scarred hands on the wine cup symbolize experience guiding innocence. The dining car becomes a sanctuary of camaraderie amidst the dangerous journey, representing the importance of loyalty and trust.",
