                      "major_task_group_title": "Virtue",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Virtue is the quality of moral excellence, integrity, and righteousness that guides individuals to act with honor, compassion, and wisdom. It is the embodiment of ethical principles, values, and virtues that inspire individuals to lead a life of purpose, meaning, and significance. Virtue is a key principle in building character, fostering empathy, and promoting personal growth. By cultivating virtue within oneself and with others, individuals can create a harmonious and ethical environment that enables them to live with integrity and authenticity. The quality of moral excellence, integrity, and righteousness that guides individuals to act with honor, compassion, and wisdom.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Virtue is the quality of moral excellence, integrity, and righteousness that guides individuals to act with honor, compassion, and wisdom.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Meditations by Marcus Aurelius",
                        "book2": "The Art of War by Sun Tzu",
                        "book3": "The Prince by Niccolò Machiavelli",
                        "book4": "The Republic by Plato",
                        "book5": "The Analects by Confucius",
                        "book6": "The Bhagavad Gita by Vyasa",
                        "book7": "The Divine Comedy by Dante Alighieri"
                      },
