                      "major_task_group_title": "Stoic Discipline",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Stoic Discipline embraces the practice of self-mastery through reason, emotional restraint, and acceptance of life’s inevitabilities. Rooted in the ancient philosophy of Stoicism, it emphasizes cultivating inner strength, resilience, and moral clarity to remain steadfast in the face of adversity. By focusing on what lies within one’s control and letting go of what does not, individuals practicing Stoic Discipline can navigate challenges with a calm mind, unwavering resolve, and purposeful action.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Forging inner resilience by harnessing reason, perspective, and moral fortitude.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Meditations by Marcus Aurelius",
                        "book2": "Letters from a Stoic by Seneca",
                        "book3": "Discourses by Epictetus",
                        "book4": "A Guide to the Good Life by William B. Irvine",
                        "book5": "The Daily Stoic by Ryan Holiday and Stephen Hanselman",
                        "book6": "How to Think Like a Roman Emperor by Donald J. Robertson",
                        "book7": "Enchiridion by Epictetus"
                      },
