                            {
                              "scene_number": 2,
                              "title": "Sanctuary Building",
                              "setup": "Recognizing the community's need for safe refuge, Francisco intentionally creates physical and emotional sanctuary spaces where people can heal from the ongoing conflict",
                              "symbolism": "Hearth as sacred center—domestic space transformed into spiritual sanctuary through intentional care",
                              "beat_goal": "Develop Francisco's practice of creating safe spaces as both practical necessity and spiritual discipline",
                              "pov": "3rd Person Limited",
                              "tense": "Past Tense",
                              "core_emotion": "Purposeful care with protective tenderness",
                              "scene_tone": "Intentional, nurturing, quietly powerful",
                              "pages": "Page 396 - 400",
                              "description": "Francisco works with the community to transform a damaged courtyard into a sanctuary garden. But it's more than physical rebuilding—he teaches them to make the space sacred through intention. Soft lighting, comfortable seating arranged for easy conversation, herbs planted for their calming scents. He creates 'comfort rituals': evening tea circles where stories are shared without pressure, quiet corners for solitary restoration, spaces designed for the specific ways people need to heal. The community recognizes this as different from mere reconstruction—it's sanctuary-making as spiritual practice.",
                              "focus": "Francisco's intentional creation of physical and emotional safe spaces as essential practice for community healing",
