                              "title": "Foundation Renewed",
                              "setup": "Through the practice of creating and maintaining sanctuary, Francisco and his community discover that these moments of shelter provide the emotional foundation for renewed hope and the courage to continue their transformative work",
                              "symbolism": "The cup replenished—emotional reserves restored through domestic bliss enabling return to cosmic service",
                              "beat_goal": "Demonstrate how sanctuary practice transforms from survival tactic into renewable source of strength and hope",
                              "pov": "3rd Person Limited",
                              "tense": "Past Tense",
                              "core_emotion": "Renewed hope infused with quiet strength",
                              "scene_tone": "Reflective, empowered, gently triumphant",
                              "pages": "Page 401 - 405",
                              "description": "In the sanctuary garden at twilight, Francisco gathers with his community for their evening ritual. What began as simple survival—creating moments of peace amid chaos—has transformed into something more profound. People share not just meals but renewed vision. The rest has clarified purpose rather than dulling it. Francisco sees that maintaining sanctuary isn't retreat from their cosmic mission but the very foundation that makes it sustainable. The Ten of Cups energy anchors them: they fight not from desperation but from fullness, not to escape suffering but to extend this domestic bliss to all humanity. Their strength comes not from denying needs but from meeting them.",
