                              "preliminarySceneDescription": "Francisco and community recognize that sanctuary practice has transformed them—not weakened by rest but strengthened, not distracted by comfort but clarified in purpose, ready for trials ahead",
                              "sensoryDetail": "Twilight garden bathed in gentle lantern glow, community circled around shared meal with faces peaceful rather than haggard, sound of genuine laughter carrying hope, taste of simple food made sacred by gratitude, sense of collective strength renewed through mutual care, stars emerging overhead connecting domestic sanctuary to cosmic purpose",
                              "internalConflict": "Francisco's lingering guilt about 'taking time' for comfort dissolving into understanding that this is how warriors stay warriors, how visionaries maintain vision, how humans serve cosmic purposes while remaining human",
                              "characterGrowthElement": "Francisco integrating the wisdom that sustainable service requires honoring all human needs—not transcending them but fulfilling them as foundation for transcendence",
                              "seriesConnectionResonance": "This understanding that cosmic work requires domestic grounding becomes Francisco's teaching throughout Books 7-9, preventing his followers from the burnout and loss of humanity that undermines so many movements",
                              "sceneCardProgression": 320,
                              "realWorldContext": "12/01/1347 Twilight—sanctuary ritual marking transformation from survival to foundation",
