                            {
                              "scene_number": 3,
                              "title": "The Victory March",
                              "setup": "With passion rekindled and voices united, the movement makes its renewed commitment public through a powerful demonstration that becomes the Six of Wands moment of triumph and recognition",
                              "symbolism": "Six of Wands triumphant—public recognition and celebration of the movement's renewed strength and unity",
                              "beat_goal": "Culminate the rally with public demonstration that solidifies commitment and attracts new supporters",
                              "pov": "3rd Person Limited",
                              "tense": "Past Tense",
                              "core_emotion": "Triumphant solidarity with powerful hope",
                              "scene_tone": "Celebratory, powerful, inspiring",
                              "pages": "Page 416 - 420",
                              "description": "At sunset, the united movement processes through Bologna's streets—not in militant march but in joyful demonstration of renewed purpose. Francisco leads but walks among them rather than above. They carry symbols of their diverse approaches woven into unified display: research scrolls, sanctuary gardens in miniature, vision-maps of the future. Citizens who'd lost hope watch, then join. The procession becomes impromptu celebration—what began as internal rally becomes public inspiration. The Six of Wands fully manifests: Francisco lifted on supporters' shoulders not as ego display but as symbol that their shared vision has a living embodiment. They're not just fighting darkness—they're demonstrating the light.",
                              "focus": "Public demonstration that transforms internal unity into visible movement, inspiring broader community and cementing commitment",
                              "chapterSceneFocus": "Ch108S3: The Victory March makes the movement's renewal visible, inspiring the broader community and attracting new allies",
                              "preliminarySceneFocus": "Public triumph and recognition",
                              "preliminarySceneDescription": "Six of Wands energy reaches culmination as renewed movement demonstrates its strength publicly, transforming from struggling resistance into victorious inspiration that draws others to the cause",
                              "sensoryDetail": "Sunset light golden on diverse banners representing different factions now unified, sound of hundreds of feet in coordinated procession, songs rising spontaneously celebrating different aspects of the work, citizens emerging from doorways drawn by the energy, children running alongside with excited faces, Francisco hoisted on shoulders with arms spread wide encompassing all rather than claiming glory, scent of hope palpable in air",
                              "internalConflict": "Francisco's discomfort with personal elevation balanced by understanding that movements need visible symbols, worry that public visibility makes them target versus recognition that hiding implies shame or doubt, humility about his role warring with acceptance that embodying the vision serves the cause",
                              "characterGrowthElement": "Francisco integrating that being the movement's symbolic center doesn't mean claiming sole credit—he can be both humble about his role and willing to stand as visible embodiment when that serves collective purpose",
                              "seriesConnectionResonance": "This public demonstration establishes pattern for how Francisco's movement will spread—not through force or secrecy but through visible joyful embodiment of alternative that attracts rather than coerces, crucial for global transformation of Books 7-9",
                              "sceneCardProgression": 323,
                              "realWorldContext": "12/03/1347 Sunset—public victory march following day of internal renewal",
                              "timelineSignificance": "Turning point when Francisco's movement shifts from hidden resistance to visible alternative, marking transition from survival mode to transformative presence",
                              "saveTheCatBeat": "Pinch - turning conflict into visible triumph",
                              "narrative_function": "Public triumph and movement expansion establishing visible transformative presence",
                              "timeline_date": "12/03/1347 - Sunset of Victory",
                              "timeline_variant": "Baseline Reality (Francisco's home timeline)",
                              "location": "Streets of Bologna, Rallying Ground",
                              "sudowrite_metadata": {
                                "intensity": "very_high",
                                "pacing": "celebratory_sweeping",
                                "narrative_mode": "triumphant_inspiration",
                                "emotional_arc": "internal_renewal_manifesting_as_public_transformation"
                              },
                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Movements gain power when they make their vision visible through joyful demonstration rather than hiding in fear",
                                "Public symbols and embodied leadership serve collective purpose when they represent shared vision rather than individual ego",
                                "Visible alternatives attract support more effectively than arguments—showing the light inspires more than condemning the darkness"
                              ],
                              "foreshadowing_elements": [
                                "This victory march becomes template for how transformation spreads—visible joyful alternatives attracting organic support",
                                "Francisco's willingness to be public symbol while maintaining humility sets tone for his global leadership",
                                "The unified display of diverse approaches foreshadows the integrated global movement of Books 7-9"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
