                          "summary": "Following the successful mediation of internal conflicts, Francisco establishes protective boundaries - both physical and psychological - to safeguard his vision and his people. These boundaries protect against external threats while maintaining internal harmony. Francisco learns that healthy boundaries are essential for sustainable community.",
                          "pov": "3rd Person Limited",
                          "tense": "Past Tense",
                          "core_emotion": "Varies by scene context",
                          "scene_tone": "Reflective and purposeful",
                          "scenes": [
                            {
                              "scene_number": 1,
                              "title": "The Vulnerable Threshold",
                              "setup": "Francisco discovers that the coalition's hard-won openness and vulnerability have created exploitable weaknesses—external forces attempt to infiltrate disguised as seekers, draining resources through manufactured crises, and gathering intelligence under pretense of joining the mission",
                              "symbolism": "The Four of Swords—strategic retreat and rest, the armored knight recuperating to fight another day, boundaries as necessary protection not rejection",
                              "beat_goal": "Establish the recognition that openness without boundaries creates vulnerability, forcing Francisco to confront the difficult truth that not all who come seeking entry have pure intentions",
                              "pov": "3rd Person Limited",
                              "tense": "Past Tense",
                              "core_emotion": "Betrayal meeting wisdom, openness learning discernment",
                              "scene_tone": "Sobering and necessary, protective awakening",
                              "pages": "Page 496 - 500",
                              "description": "The warning comes from Sophia, whose mystical sensitivity detects something wrong in three 'seekers' who joined after hearing of Francisco's magnetic presence. Her intuition—what de Becker would call the gift of fear—registers subtle signals that conscious analysis misses: questions that probe tactical information rather than spiritual seeking, energy that takes rather than exchanges, patterns that suggest coordination rather than spontaneous arrival. When Francisco investigates, the pattern becomes clear: their hard-won transparency and vulnerability, so essential for authentic community, have created exploitable access. One 'seeker' is gathering intelligence for temporal mages threatened by Francisco's alternative approach. Another manufactures crises requiring resources, systematically draining the coalition's capacity. A third probes for divisions to exploit, attempting to reignite the Elena-Marcus conflict they worked so hard to heal. Francisco faces a painful recognition: the openness that enabled authentic connection also enabled infiltration. His first instinct—closing everything down, trusting no one—would destroy the very community he's trying to protect. But continuing without boundaries would allow the community to be systematically undermined. The Four of Swords energy manifests not as permanent retreat but as strategic rest and recuperation—pulling back to assess, creating protected space to heal and plan, establishing boundaries that allow for both openness and protection. When he shares the discovery with his core circle, Elena's response cuts to the heart: 'We created a home. We forgot that homes need doors—not to keep everyone out, but to control who enters and on what terms.' The scene ends with Francisco recognizing that mature community requires not just unity and diversity navigation but also wise boundary-setting that protects without isolating, discriminates without prejudice, and maintains integrity while remaining accessible to authentic seekers.",
                              "focus": "Francisco's painful recognition that openness without boundaries creates vulnerability, requiring development of discernment and protective structures",
                              "chapterSceneFocus": "Ch114S1: Francisco discovers coalition's openness has been exploited, forcing recognition that boundaries are necessary protection not betrayal of values",
                              "preliminarySceneFocus": "Vulnerability requiring protection",
                              "preliminarySceneDescription": "The Four of Swords recognizes that strategic retreat and boundary-setting are necessary for long-term sustainability and protection",
                              "sensoryDetail": "The quality of Sophia's disquiet—not dramatic but persistent, like a wrong note in familiar music; the three infiltrators' energy feeling subtly extractive, taking more than giving in energetic exchanges; the visual of Francisco's face as recognition dawns—pain mixing with necessity; the weight of betrayal settling in the room as the core circle processes the infiltration; the texture of innocence lost—their earlier naive openness giving way to wiser discernment; the sound of Elena's voice cutting through with uncomfortable truth about homes needing doors; the chill of recognizing how close they came to being systematically undermined; Francisco's gut responding to intuition he'd previously ignored in favor of radical acceptance",
                              "internalConflict": "Francisco's deep resistance to boundaries warring with recognition of their necessity—his fear that any limitation betrays the radical openness that enabled community versus awareness that unlimited access enables exploitation, his struggle between wanting to trust everyone and needing to develop discernment, his grief over losing a certain innocence about human nature",
                              "characterGrowthElement": "Francisco learning that mature community requires boundaries as much as openness—discovering that protection and connection aren't opposites but complements, that discernment isn't judgment but wisdom, that saying 'no' to some enables deeper 'yes' to others, beginning to develop the self-protection skills essential for sustainable leadership",
                              "seriesConnectionResonance": "Establishes the boundary-setting wisdom essential for Books 7-9 when humanity's awakening must be protected from forces that would exploit or corrupt the transformation—Francisco's learning to balance openness with discernment becomes template for how evolved consciousness protects itself without becoming closed or rigid",
                              "sceneCardProgression": 339,
                              "realWorldContext": "12/23/1347 Evening—Bologna's diverse communities watching Francisco's coalition with mixture of inspiration and predatory interest—the coalition's success attracting both authentic seekers and those who would exploit or undermine",
                              "timelineSignificance": "The moment when naive openness must evolve into wise discernment through painful recognition of exploitation",
                              "saveTheCatBeat": "Converge (resolution) - recognizing need for protective boundaries",
                              "narrativeFunction": "Establishing the necessity of boundaries through painful recognition of exploitation, initiating Francisco's boundary-setting development",
                              "timeline_date": "12/23/1347 - Innocence Lost",
                              "timeline_variant": "Baseline Reality (Francisco's home timeline)",
