                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Structure pitch with clear narrative journey—Cicero's awakening story (consciousness in Rome, terror discovering death, centuries developing rhetoric, hope finding allies) demonstrates three-act arc with emotional progression creating investment independent of logical argument (Gallo: stories activate brain differently than facts, narrative journey with protagonist struggle and resolution generates empathy and buy-in)",
                                "Incorporate emotional hooks early—Cicero sharing terror discovering predetermined death at story opening creates immediate emotional connection before philosophical content, anchoring listeners via feeling not reasoning (Gallo: emotional hooks within first minute determine whether audience stays engaged, vulnerability and universal emotions create bonding that rational argument cannot)",
                                "Draft 3-minute narrative pitch—Collective members practicing condensed rebellion story with clear journey, emotional hooks, vivid examples demonstrates that complex philosophical arguments translate into compelling narratives when structured with story principles (Gallo: constraint forcing brevity and clarity improves message retention, testing pitch iterations with listener feedback reveals emotional resonance patterns)"
                              ],
