                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Map stakeholder emotions in key scenarios—creating empathy maps for three recruit archetypes (Grief/Philosophy/Heritage-Motivated) identifying what they see/hear/think/feel/fear/desire enables differentiated compassionate approaches (Ross: stakeholder emotion mapping reveals diverse needs requiring tailored responses, systematic empathy understanding drives effective relationship-building, mapping prevents projection enabling authentic connection)",
                                "Design empathetic customer journeys—recognizing Grief-Motivated need Empathy Circles first while Philosophy-Motivated need Golden Circle clarity demonstrates journey design serving diverse needs (Ross: empathetic journeys match offerings to stakeholder emotional states, one-size-fits-all approaches miss opportunities for connection, differentiated pathways respect diversity while maintaining coherent values)",
                                "Embed empathy metrics into performance reviews—measuring recruitment effectiveness by archetype fit and trust-building not just numbers (Ross: empathy metrics make emotional intelligence organizationally accountable, tracking relationship quality alongside quantity, embedding empathy measurement into evaluation reinforces it as strategic priority not optional nicety)"
