                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Conduct integrity audits of commitments—rebellion's credibility audit assessing whether values (cultural autonomy, collective consciousness) actually guide decisions reveals integrity strength creating trust foundation (Covey: integrity means walking talk, auditing commitment-action alignment exposes gaps preventing credibility erosion, consistent values-behavior match builds foundational trustworthiness)",
                                "Demonstrate competence via small wins—Francisco implementing incremental results strategy versus promising major cosmic authority victories shows capability through achievable demonstrations (Covey: credibility requires proving competence through results not claims, small wins build trust as track record accumulates, capability demonstration should match actual capacity preventing overpromise-underdeliver trust destruction)",
                                "Use swift apologies and corrections when mistakes occur—Francisco's immediate credibility gap addressing (intent-clarification vulnerability, capability-building protocols) versus defensiveness demonstrates repair commitment (Covey: trustSpeed increases when mistakes acknowledged and fixed swiftly, defensive justification erodes credibility while transparent correction strengthens it, swift repair shows integrity through accountability)"
