                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Take responsibility for team results publicly—Francisco's Extreme Ownership declaration ('this failure is entirely my responsibility') versus defensive blame-sharing demonstrates absolute accountability enabling learning (Willink & Babin: leaders own all outcomes refusing excuses, public responsibility-taking models accountability inspiring team ownership, deflection-free accountability creates trust and learning foundation)",
                                "Develop contingency plans for key risks—mandatory protocols implemented after Milan failure (contingency planning, timeline development with input, security certification, risk briefings) prevent recurrence (Willink & Babin: contingency planning demonstrates proactive ownership anticipating failure modes, protocols embed accountability preventing repeated mistakes, systematic risk planning shows genuine ownership versus reactive blame)",
                                "Debrief failures with root-cause analysis—after-action review examining what supposed to happen, what happened, why, what differently transforms failure into systemic learning (Willink & Babin: root-cause analysis prevents surface-level fixes missing underlying issues, supposed-actual-why-differently framework creates actionable improvements, systematic debriefing culture makes failure valuable learning opportunity)"
                              ],
