                      "major_task_group_title": "Considered Reform",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Considered Reform highlights the deliberate, thoughtful evaluation of systems, policies, or practices in order to pinpoint opportunities for genuine improvement. By integrating empirical research, stakeholder feedback, and ethical imperatives, this approach prioritizes both the root causes and the practical implications of transformative change. Above all, it underscores that sustainable reform requires methodical planning, inclusive dialogue, and a commitment to ethical principles—ensuring that progress is both meaningful and resilient in the face of complexity.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Driving meaningful change through deliberate, inclusive, and ethically guided transformation.",
