                              },
                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Set a clear 'bright-spot' goal for the team—celebrating memory anchor successes and temporal redundancy wins provides evidence-based hope demonstrating what's working (Heath & Heath: bright-spots show solutions already succeeding, highlighting wins provides concrete evidence change is possible, focusing on successes creates replicable models versus problem-fixation paralysis)",
                                "Map the path by removing friction—providing memory anchor templates and temporal redundancy tools transforms complexity into accessible action enabling broader participation (Heath & Heath: friction removal eliminates obstacles preventing action, clear simple tools accelerate adoption, mapping the path makes abstract goals concrete and achievable)",
                                "Celebrate early victories to build momentum—publicly recognizing members whose innovations protected comrades creates success modeling inspiring replication and team confidence (Heath & Heath: celebration reinforces desired behaviors, early wins demonstrate progress building momentum, public recognition creates social proof motivating broader adoption)"
                              ],
