                              "learning_objectives": [
                                "Use multi-track decision-making in crises—parallel exploration (evacuation logistics + defensive preparations + counter-weapon development) enables faster discovery than sequential analysis (Heath & Heath: multi-tracking explores multiple paths simultaneously, parallel development reveals interactions between options, distributed effort reduces all-or-nothing risk of single approach)",
                                "Flip the decision frame under time constraints—changing question ('what to protect' → 'what authorities fear most') reveals solutions invisible in original framing (Heath & Heath: frame-flipping shifts perspective uncovering new possibilities, reframing question often more valuable than answering it, perspective changes reveal previously hidden options)",
