                                "Design 'stress-based' mini-experiments—Marcus's simulation testing pruning versus addition outcomes (40%→15% versus 40%→60%) provides quantified risk assessment (Taleb: stress-testing reveals system fragilities under pressure, experimentation validates counterintuitive approaches before full commitment, evidence-based evaluation beats intuitive assumptions)",
