                              "timelineSignificance": "Rebellion's balanced boldness framework (systematic three-step protocol integrating Kahneman/Taleb/Holiday) creating decisional evolution—transformation from impulsive rushing (Scene 1 trap creating crisis) to framework-guided sustainable courage (preventing future errors while maintaining bold action capability), establishing Books 5-9 comprehensive decision-making infrastructure cosmic authorities' reactive adaptations cannot anticipate.",
                              "saveTheCatBeat": "Allies - integrating mentor wisdom (Adriana, Marcus, Sofia) into comprehensive sustainable framework",
                              "narrativeFunction": "Completes Allies, Mentors, and Helpers (integrating mentor wisdom into sustainable approach) by demonstrating balanced boldness framework—72-hour arc assessment (Scene 1 System 1 trap + 23 disbanded cells cost, Scene 2 Via Negativa pruning reducing exposure, Scene 3 Perception reframing capturing Milan/Naples/Palermo) revealing net strategic gain purchased at price. Shows framework integration: advisory council synthesis (Adriana emphasizing System 1/System 2 balance, Marcus highlighting Via Negativa power, Sofia noting Perception transformation) creating comprehensive approach—Kahneman + Taleb + Holiday forming balanced boldness. Proposes three-step protocol: (1) System 1/System 2 Classification (intuition versus deliberation?), (2) Via Negativa Audit (fragilities to remove first?), (3) Perception Scan (obstacles as opportunities?) systematizing foresight before bold action. Validates via retrospective: applying to Scene 1 would have flagged archive strike requiring deliberation, identified trackable connections as fragilities, reframed suspicious timing. Completes Page of Wands maturity: enthusiasm guided by wisdom. Manifests Han Purple fully: transformative maturity balancing urgency with prudence. Establishes decisional evolution—bold yet mindful movement. Ends chapter with sustainable courage framework setting up Books 5-9 systematic decision quality.",
