                                "saveTheCatBeat": "Tests, Allies, Enemies - beginning resilience via long-term grit commitment",
                                "narrativeFunction": "Begins Tests, Allies, Enemies resilience phase (building psychological endurance) by introducing siege challenge—authorities launching Endurance Siege (18-month to 5-year multi-front pressure) testing grit versus enthusiasm. Demonstrates Duckworth's Grit Passion and Perseverance: Francisco recognizing capability-resilience gap (integrated advantage useless if unsustainable under prolonged pressure), proposing Long-Range Passion Project (30-month Resilience Marathon treating siege as training), establishing three components (Daily Effort Tracking, Monthly Milestones, Year-Long Challenges), observing 90-day paradox (pressure increasing commitment, compounding gains, setback immunity). Shows that sustained effort outperforms intensity—grit creating endurance enthusiasm cannot. Introduces Eight of Cups: strength via strategic abandonment. Deepens London Hue: sustained pressure capacity maturity. Begins resilience Tests. Sets up Scene 2 exploring emotional navigation and Scene 3 building resilience systems. Plants foundation for Books 4-9 endurance-based strength.",
