                      "major_task_group_title": "Economic Prudence",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Economic Prudence underscores the deliberate and responsible management of financial and material resources to foster sustainable growth and stability. By balancing short-term needs with long-term objectives, individuals and communities can avoid unnecessary debt, invest wisely, and build secure foundations for future opportunities. Through careful planning, disciplined execution, and ethical consideration, Economic Prudence lays the groundwork for resilience amid uncertain markets and evolving economic landscapes.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Strengthening prosperity through measured stewardship and strategic foresight.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "The Intelligent Investor by Benjamin Graham",
