                      "major_task_group_title": "Psychological Resilience",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Psychological Resilience highlights the internal processes that enable individuals to adapt positively in the face of stress, adversity, or trauma. By developing coping strategies, emotional regulation skills, and a growth mindset, one can maintain a steady sense of well-being and effectively navigate life’s uncertainties. Cultivating psychological resilience fosters confidence, mental agility, and the capacity to emerge stronger from challenging experiences.",
