                      "major_task_group_title": "(Impulse) Karma",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Karma symbolizes the principle of cause and effect, highlighting how our actions, impulses, and intentions inevitably shape the realities we experience. By practicing mindfulness, accountability, and ethical reflection, individuals acknowledge the ripple effects of their decisions on themselves and those around them. Embracing Karma in daily life involves cultivating positive habits, honoring moral responsibilities, and learning from the consequences of missteps to progress on a path of authenticity, growth, and compassionate engagement.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Harnessing the law of cause and effect to deepen ethical awareness and transform daily living.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Karma: A Yogi’s Guide to Crafting Your Destiny by Sadhguru",
                        "book2": "The Power of Habit by Charles Duhigg",
                        "book3": "The Book of Joy by Dalai Lama and Desmond Tutu",
                        "book4": "Mindfulness in Plain English by Bhante Gunaratana",
                        "book5": "Living Your Yoga: Finding the Spiritual in Everyday Life by Judith Hanson Lasater",
                        "book6": "Ethics for the New Millennium by the Dalai Lama",
                        "book7": "When Things Fall Apart by Pema Chödrön"
                      },
