                      "major_task_group_title": "Stoic Resilience",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Stoic Resilience emphasizes enduring adversity with calm and fortitude by applying ancient Stoic principles to modern life. By focusing on what lies within one’s control and letting go of external events or outcomes, individuals strengthen their emotional stability and gain mental clarity. Stoic Resilience nurtures virtues such as self-discipline, patience, and courage, enabling people to endure challenges with composure and wisdom, while maintaining a sense of purpose and moral integrity.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Enduring adversity with a calm mind, fortified by the timeless virtues of Stoicism.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Meditations by Marcus Aurelius",
                        "book2": "Discourses and Selected Writings by Epictetus",
                        "book3": "Letters from a Stoic by Seneca",
                        "book4": "A Guide to the Good Life by William B. Irvine",
                        "book5": "How to Think Like a Roman Emperor by Donald J. Robertson",
                        "book6": "The Practicing Stoic by Ward Farnsworth",
                        "book7": "Lives of the Stoics by Ryan Holiday and Stephen Hanselman"
                      },
