                      "red": "176",
                      "green": "228",
                      "blue": "255",
                      "major_task_group_title": "Existential Reflection",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Existential Reflection encourages deep introspection into life’s ultimate questions: Who are we, why are we here, and how should we navigate existence in a universe that may appear indifferent to our concerns? By exploring philosophical, spiritual, and psychological perspectives on meaning, purpose, and mortality, individuals can gain a clearer sense of self, clarify their values, and find renewed motivation to shape a life of authenticity. Emphasizing curiosity and honesty, Existential Reflection challenges people to confront uncertainty and discover personal truths to guide them through life’s complexities.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Contemplating life’s meaning to anchor one’s identity, purpose, and way of being.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Man’s Search for Meaning by Viktor E. Frankl",
                        "book2": "The Myth of Sisyphus by Albert Camus",
                        "book3": "Being and Nothingness by Jean-Paul Sartre",
                        "book4": "At the Existentialist Café by Sarah Bakewell",
                        "book5": "The Denial of Death by Ernest Becker",
                        "book6": "Staring at the Sun by Irvin D. Yalom",
                        "book7": "When Things Fall Apart by Pema Chödrön"
                      },
