                      "major_task_group_title": "Play - Abandon",
                      "major_task_group_description": "Play - Abandon highlights the importance of embracing spontaneity, freedom, and uninhibited expression. It encourages individuals to let go of constraints, self-judgment, and overthinking, allowing creativity and joy to flourish. By tapping into our innate capacity for play, we can discover new perspectives, restore our energy, and strengthen our relationships through genuine connection and shared laughter. Play - Abandon fosters resilience and adaptability, reminding us that unstructured play is an essential component of personal growth and well-being.",
                      "major_task_group_tagline": "Embrace spontaneity, freedom, and uninhibited expression for deeper joy and self-discovery.",
                      "major_task_group_books_influenced_by": {
                        "book1": "Play: How It Shapes the Brain, Opens the Imagination, and Invigorates the Soul by Stuart Brown",
                        "book2": "Free to Learn by Peter Gray",
                        "book3": "Big Magic: Creative Living Beyond Fear by Elizabeth Gilbert",
                        "book4": "The Art of Possibility by Rosamund Stone Zander and Benjamin Zander",
                        "book5": "Flow: The Psychology of Optimal Experience by Mihaly Csikszentmihalyi",
                        "book6": "The Gifts of Imperfection by Brené Brown",
                        "book7": "Improv Wisdom: Don’t Prepare, Just Show Up by Patricia Ryan Madson"
                      },
